<title>TURKEY: Turkish H1 company earnings forecasts -- poll.</title>
<headline>Turkish H1 company earnings forecasts -- poll.</headline>
<byline>Birsen Altayli</byline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkish companies, their share performance overshadowed recently by political uncertainty, will show mixed earnings performances for the first half of 1997, according to a Reuters survey of six brokerage firms.</p>
<p>In the poll on net profit expectations for the leading 68 companies listed on the Istanbul stock exchange, Ekinciler Investment and Securities research director Ercument Istemi said he expected the cement, banking and energy sectors to show the best earnings performance in the six-month period.</p>
<p>&quot;Among these sectors, a 15-percent dollar rise in cement prices is likely to have contributed to a rise in net profits in the second quarter,&quot; Istemi told Reuters.</p>
<p>In the energy sector, he said &quot;we expect a better performance from the energy sector in the second quarter on the assumption of a 10- to 12-percent rise in energy demand and a monthly three-percent rise in electricity prices in the remainder of the year.&quot;</p>
<p>In the banking sector, Istemi expected Akbank in particular was to show positive results.</p>
<p>Fuat Erbil, head of research at Interyatirim, forecasts good performances from companies involved in white goods, commercial vehicles, foodstuffs, paints and plastics and cement.</p>
<p>Poor performances were expected from the beer, paper, media and textile sectors, Erbil said.</p>
<p>Six brokerages' forecasts of first-half net earnings for 68 listed companies are as follows:</p>
<p>1- Interyatirim, 2- General Finans, 3- Evis Securities, 4-Bayindir Securities, 5- Demir Investment, 6- Ekinciler Investment and Securities.</p>
